But note that load_container_onto_leg also requires candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_transport_leg_linked ?candidate ?transport_leg, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_available ?loading_container, transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg, not loading_container_loaded ?loading_container. So we need candidate_prepared for beta, candidate_transport_leg_linked (we have from init), candidate_loading_container_linked (we have for beta with loading_container_beta), loading_container_available (we have beta), transport_leg_assembled and loading_authorized (we will have after assembling leg and authorizing). Good.

Thus we need to have transport leg assembled and loading authorized before we can load container for beta. However loading container onto leg will set loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked. After that, we can stage candidate (requires loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked). Good.

