cating to second candidate. So we need to dispatch each candidate before reusing its vehicle.

Thus we need to dispatch each candidate before we can reuse its vehicle for another candidate. Since we have only three vehicles, we need to dispatch at least one candidate before allocating vehicle to the fourth.

We have four candidates needing vehicle: alpha schedule, beta schedule, origin, destination. We can dispatch three of them (freeing vehicles) and then allocate the fourth using a freed vehicle.

Thus we need to interleave allocations and dispatches.

Goal requires dispatched shift_candidate_alpha, origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha. So those three must be dispatched. Shift_candidate_beta does NOT need to be dispatched (only staged). So we can dispatch the three required ones, freeing their vehicles, then allocate vehicle to beta for staging (using the now-available vehicle). Good.

