Thus plan:

- Prepare origin, assign operator, activate node, lock, then release operator.
- Prepare destination, assign operator, activate node, lock, release operator.
- Assemble leg, authorize loading.
- Mark origin dispatch ready, destination dispatch ready.
- Allocate dispatch slot for origin, execute origin dispatch (vehicle allocated earlier; after dispatch vehicle becomes available).
- Allocate dispatch slot for destination, execute destination dispatch.
- Now operator is free (we released after lock). Good.

- Prepare shift_candidate_alpha: create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm prepared, assign operator, assign compliance cert, apply operational constraint, confirm operator alignment, verify compliance, finalize after compliance, allocate dispatch slot, execute schedule dispatch, release operator? Not needed after dispatch maybe but we will release operator after dispatch to free for beta.

